\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 #\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 Courses: master plan\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Status: plan, for iteration\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Last updated: 2026-07-26\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Parent: site-audit-and-audience-plan.md (sections 0, 5, 6, 6b, 10)\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Children: still-yourself-course-draft.md (production draft), clarity-course-draft_2.md (origin record)\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 This doc holds the family: what qualifies as one of my courses, how they relate, what format they take, and how the published articles feed them. It points at the drafts rather than repeating them.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 1. The test\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 A course is mine if it passes three checks. If it fails any of them it is someone else's product and I should not build it.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **It teaches judgment, not mechanics.** Mechanics depreciate as models improve. Judgment, curation, and teaching appreciate. Nothing about how to use a tool.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **It uses the mechanic.** You notice, you write one line in your own words, you leave with a page nobody handed you. That mechanic is the format signature across every course. If a course would work as a lecture, it is not one of these.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **It comes from a seat I actually occupy.** Working design leader, mid-career, running an agentic practice with four reports, going through the same shift as the buyer. Not narrating from outside it.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 The through-line under all of them: taste is triage, deciding what deserves attention when anything can be made. Each course points that at a different subject.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 2. Mindfulness is the instrument, not the subject\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Settled, and it is the thing most likely to drift, so it is written down.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 I have led meditation and mindfulness sessions for years, in written scripts, at company all hands and in longer sessions. That is a credential and a method. It is not a category I sell in.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 The reason is not squeamishness, it is market position. General mindfulness content is the most commoditized material on the internet and I have no distribution advantage in it. Presence applied to a working professional's real situation, from someone standing in the same shift, is close to un-taken. As the instrument I am nearly alone. As the subject I am a newcomer in a saturated market.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Practical rules:\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 The word mindfulness never appears as a category on ramphal.design. No section, no tag, no library of recordings.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 It appears once, as a credential, in the long about page. One sentence, appended to the existing paragraph, no heading.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 Design work stays the visible anchor and the front door. The clarity work is the deeper layer for people who already trust the design voice.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 Publish at most one session as demonstration when the course exists, framed as the method behind it. Never a library.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 3. The family\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Four candidates, one axis: what the noticing is pointed at.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Course | Points at | Buyer | Status |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 |---|---|---|---|\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Still Yourself | You | Mid-career professional feeling the ground move | Production draft written |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Taste Is Triage | The work | Designers and design leads | Outlined, article live |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | The Room | Your team | New design leads and managers | Concept, raw material exists |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Still Leading | You as a leader | Leads unsteady during a shift | Folded in, do not launch |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **Still Yourself is the trunk, not a sibling.** It is the general case and it establishes the mechanic and the session shape. Write it properly once and the others get cheaper, because they inherit the format. It is also the furthest from the design anchor, so it is the one that most needs the design work visible in front of it.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **Still Leading overlaps Still Yourself and The Room from both sides.** Four courses for what is really two buyers is fragmentation. Ship it as a two or three session extension of Still Yourself for people with reports.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **The Room is the home for the team dynamics material.** Those old written courses are work content, not clarity content, and they fit the design leadership brand with zero whiplash. Keep them out of Still Yourself entirely.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 4. Format: written, self-led, paced\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **Written is the product. Audio is an option added later. No video.**\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Written wins on cost to revise, it lives in the vault, it is searchable and accessible, and it clears the cringe threshold: a skeptical senior professional will read something private that they would never press play on.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Video was considered and rejected. The timer it adds is a progress bar, and a progress bar turns a silence into a countdown. It also forces a decision about what is on screen during the silence, where every option is bad: a face waiting is unwatchable, a black card is audio with a camera bill, and ambient b-roll is the retreat brochure. Video also has the highest cringe threshold of the three.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 What written loses is pace control, and pace control is most of the point. It gets rebuilt in the interface, not the medium:\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 One beat per screen.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 The continue control disabled for the length of the silence.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 The line prompt appears only after the pause has actually run.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 The page (the artifact) delivered as a printable sheet and a plain markdown file. Nothing app-shaped, because tools that need hand-feeding get abandoned.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Audio per session comes after the text is proven, for people who want to close their eyes. Written stays canonical, audio is derived, same rule as the essays.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 5. The archive\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 All written scripts, not recordings. No transcription needed, no participant privacy issue, and it merges directly into the drafts because it is already in the right medium.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Material | Use |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 |---|---|\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Short all-hands breaks | Source for the arrive beat. That wording repeats in all six sessions and has to be right. Years of tested versions exist, on a room that did not choose to be there. |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Longer sessions | Source for prompt phrasings and for how I hold a silence. Look for phrasings reused without planning to, unplanned repetition is the real material. |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 | Team dynamics courses | Not clarity content. Feeds The Room, or a paid workshop. Keep separate. |\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Method, so this does not become a project: do not read them all. Pick the ones remembered as going well, and extract only three things, openings, prompt phrasings, and closes. Those transfer. The bodies are welded to their topic and will not move.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Conversion caveat: a script written to be read to a room assumes I control the pace and speaks to a group. Self-led text hands pacing to the reader and speaks to one person. Rewrite deliberately, do not paste.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Hard rule: the archive does not set the agenda. The six-session arc is settled. A strong session on another subject is a note for later, not a seventh session. Same sunk-asset trap as the video question.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 6. The articles are the on-ramps\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Both tracks already have a live front door. This is the piece that changes the sequencing.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **Taste Is Triage** (/doc/taste-is-triage, Jul 2026) is live and is the flagship. The because is explicit, the Chanel subtraction rule is the strongest paragraph, the cow line is the quotable. It closes on the craft framing, so it feeds track one.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 **Friction** (/doc/friction, tagged career and mindset) sits with a fear rather than resolving it, which makes it the natural on-ramp for Still Yourself.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Rule from the parent plan, now with actual pages attached: match the call to action to the essay's register. Craft essays point to Taste Is Triage. Introspective essays point to Still Yourself. Until the courses exist, both point at the list.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Open gaps on the live site, in priority order:\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 1. \cf4 \strokec4 **No subscribe capture anywhere.** The flagship closes with "come along" and there is nothing to click. An invitation with no door on it. Cheapest, highest-leverage fix available.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 2. \cf4 \strokec4 **Homepage prerender is stale.** The no-JS homepage lists three articles and does not include the flagship, so crawlers and agents see a homepage that does not know it exists.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 3. \cf4 \strokec4 **Per-article meta title** falls back to the generic site title.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 4. \cf4 \strokec4 **13 versus 15 years.** The homepage says 13, the flagship body and meta say fifteen. Pick one.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 7. Sequencing\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 The trunk is the right thing to write first and the wrong thing to launch first, because it is furthest from the anchor.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 1. \cf4 \strokec4 **Now:** subscribe capture on Taste Is Triage and Friction. Fix the homepage prerender. Let the flagship run a few weeks. If the anchor essay does not pull, a course built on it will not either, and that is cheap to learn.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 2. \cf4 \strokec4 **Next:** finish Still Yourself as the format bible. Voice pass against the archive. Build the paced-reveal reader for one session and test it on myself.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 3. \cf4 \strokec4 **Then:** launch Taste Is Triage first, off the live article, as the same idea expanded. Keep the name identical to the article, article is the free front door, course is the expansion.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 4. \cf4 \strokec4 **Then:** Still Yourself, sold to the list that the introspective essays built.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 5. \cf4 \strokec4 **Later:** The Room, from the team dynamics material.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 ---\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ##\cf4 \strokec4  \cf2 \strokec2 8. Open calls\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 Write session 1 of Still Yourself in my own voice, using the archive openings, then leave it a week and read it cold. If the first two minutes do not make me feel seen, nothing else gets built.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 Decide where the paced reader lives. Ghost, or a small static thing I own.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 Decide the 13 versus 15 number and apply it everywhere at once.\cb1 \
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 - \cf4 \strokec4 The coherence line still needs one home, said once: taste is triage applied to a person instead of a product, and you cannot triage while panicking. Currently implicit in session 4.\cb1 \
}